{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat","id":895616,"title":"Invisibility & Combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-21T12:07:14-07:00","id":895616,"title":"Invisibility & Combat?","content":"I've been looking through some of the Rote after the initial &quot;oh-my-Gods-it-is-out&quot; feelings had settled, and some thoughts occurred when reading the Invisibility Rote p. 143.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Warning: Do attempt this with Sleepers present</span><br /> As I've understood, all spells follow the same rules; 1 Potency, an arms reach in size, 1 turns duration, ect.. Unless Reach is spent. So to me, Invisibility seems rather powerful when it comes to combat. At the moment, there is no rules for how it works (that I remember). But I am imagine that the ones that are attacked or try to attack the invisible target, counts as being affected by the &quot;Blind&quot; tilt, where both eyes are affected (-5 on attack rolls and no Defense against the mage).<br /> <br /> Or is it just me that finds it powerful? Might be.. Haven't played mage that much, so maybe I just need to understand the system a little better.<br /> <br /> But I was thinking that Potency could determine how invisible you where.. But that might become to gimmicky and complicated..<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T12:35:39-07:00","id":895634,"title":"","content":"I would probably give them a beneficial Tilt/Condition that would add passive attack bonus (like, +2) and could be burned for one attack that ignores Defense. But that's me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T13:10:28-07:00","id":895654,"title":"","content":"Since defense can only be used against an expected attack I agree with @WHW that it could potentially negate defense. At least for a single turn then I'd say the condition suggested would be a good fit or just start with the tilt if the person you are attacking expects the attack from an invisible source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T01:43:16-07:00","id":895991,"title":"","content":"Hmm.. Good points. If unaware of the invisible assailant, I guess just use the ambush rules here and for acutal combat, the weaker &quot;version&quot; of Blind Tilt could work as the beneficial Tilt you mentioned since the target is at -3 to attacks and has half defense. Not nearly as punishing as I originally imagined it.<br /> <br /> I guess if someone had heightened senses, they could lower these penalties depending on how powerful the senses are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T02:20:11-07:00","id":895998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=895991#post895991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm.. Good points. If unaware of the invisible assailant, I guess just use the ambush rules here and for acutal combat, the weaker &quot;version&quot; of Blind Tilt could work as the beneficial Tilt you mentioned since the target is at -3 to attacks and has half defense. Not nearly as punishing as I originally imagined it.<br /> <br /> I guess if someone had heightened senses, they could lower these penalties depending on how powerful the senses are?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a werewolf was to use their nose to track you instead of their eyes I'd say they would potentially negate the penalties with their bonus from such senses. It wouldn't so much be lowering the penalties but rather using an advantage to break even or come out just ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T02:43:15-07:00","id":896001,"title":"","content":"I am not sure I would do that completely in the case of with werewolves, since they have various degrees of how strong their senses is. For their Urhan form; most definitely. For their Dalu form; maybe just lower the penalties. I think Gauru and Urshul might be close enough to Urhan to also negate it.<br /> <br /> It would be much simpler to just say it negates the penalty. But the Heightened Senses rote also works with degrees of senses, and I think there should be a difference between having a potency 1 and a potency 5 enhanced sense, otherwise there seems less reason to increase its potency. At least in this case.<br /> <br /> Note: first I thought there would be a Clash of Wills, but it is not the spell that is revealing the invisible mage; it is the mages Senses. Besides, Life affects the life pattern of a subject. Not its light/energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T04:27:23-07:00","id":896018,"title":"","content":"Werewolves would have no penalties fighting an invisible combatant, actually, if using wolf senses, as per page 94:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf Senses</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wolf senses are considered the werewolf's default senses in Urhan and Urshul form. Wolf senses offer a bonus to Perception-based rolls depending on her form. Further, if she would normally suffer penalties due to deprivation (blindness, strong scents, or deafness), her other senses compensate, negating those penalties entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Invisibility isn't strictly affecting the targets (and so I wouldn't probably use the full severity of the Blinded Tilt, but it'd require at least the lesser version), this seems pretty clear (ha!) to me that it would apply here. Honestly, it's not even quite as bad as a werewolf fully losing her sight, but think about it this way: The assailant is completely invisible. In terms of fighting this particular foe with sight, the werewolf might as well be in a pitch black room, right? So if the other wolf senses completely negate that penalty, they'd do so for Invisibility.<br /> <br /> Lesson: A cocksure mage who has gone invisible and thinks to get the drop on a pack of werewolves is very quickly going to be one dead mage. You'd basically have to become invisible, soundless, scentless, and then also not leave any tracks that a werewolf could use to locate you (though surely at a penalty \u2014 but they <i>are </i>peerless trackers). At which point, you've almost certainly defeated any thinking foe, provided you have a way to kill them without exposing yourself to retaliation.<br /> <br /> Then <i>again</i>, you have Gifts like Lore of the Land, Read the World's Loom, and especially Scent the Unnatural.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T06:23:55-07:00","id":896048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896001#post896001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure I would do that completely in the case of with werewolves, since they have various degrees of how strong their senses is. For their Urhan form; most definitely. For their Dalu form; maybe just lower the penalties. I think Gauru and Urshul might be close enough to Urhan to also negate it.<br /> <br /> It would be much simpler to just say it negates the penalty. But the Heightened Senses rote also works with degrees of senses, and I think there should be a difference between having a potency 1 and a potency 5 enhanced sense, otherwise there seems less reason to increase its potency. At least in this case.<br /> <br /> Note: first I thought there would be a Clash of Wills, but it is not the spell that is revealing the invisible mage; it is the mages Senses. Besides, Life affects the life pattern of a subject. Not its light/energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Claire said, plus they can reflexively get their Wolf-Senses in non-lupine shapes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T16:48:16-07:00","id":896388,"title":"","content":"My mistake on the wolf senses. Poor example I can admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T17:47:31-07:00","id":896417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896388#post896388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My mistake on the wolf senses. Poor example I can admit.</div> </div> </div> </div>No no, it's an easy thing to miss. Not everyone knows all the rules in every line perfectly. However, I figured it'd be a good time to show off what werewolves can do!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T18:16:46-07:00","id":896437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896417#post896417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No no, it's an easy thing to miss. Not everyone knows all the rules in every line perfectly. However, I figured it'd be a good time to show off what werewolves can do!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Although a moderately competent Obrimos (and anyone with a few dots in Forces) and just two dots in Life could probably evade standard werewolf senses or create so many false positives as to render it useless (some Space, Prime or Matter, or even Death to travel in ghost-frequency Twilight, also would be helpful).<br /> <br /> In fact, when dealing with werewolves, using Arcana like Forces, Life and Matter to overwhelm werewolf senses is probably a better combat tactic that stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T19:48:43-07:00","id":896479,"title":"","content":"I doubt you can overwhelm their senses. They can literally hear for miles around and they work perfectly fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T21:16:38-07:00","id":896508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896479#post896479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I doubt you can overwhelm their senses. They can literally hear for miles around and they work perfectly fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>.<br /> That's precisely the point. Even minor proficiency in Forces can create both overwhelmingly loud and focused sounds as well as multiple images and/or identical sounds and images over a wide area. It's not a matter of hearing or seeing a mage, but ascertaining which mage is the real one.<br /> <br /> Ancillary sensory input like scent can be masked by Life or duplicated with Matter, also both a lower levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T23:36:10-07:00","id":896579,"title":"","content":"Drop some marbles on the ground around yourself, create smoke screen or total darkness ... that way you are both blind and hopefully you are prepared to deal with those conditions better than your opponents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T01:38:18-07:00","id":896636,"title":"","content":"I don't see why you shouldn't be able to overwhelm the senses of something with supersenses. Or someone with normal senses for that matter. <br /> <br /> But yea, to completely evade a werewolf, you would need to do allot of hoopely jumps and snickedy sneakeeks :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:55:35-07:00","id":896719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896508#post896508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> That's precisely the point. Even minor proficiency in Forces can create both overwhelmingly loud and focused sounds as well as multiple images and/or identical sounds and images over a wide area. It's not a matter of hearing or seeing a mage, but ascertaining which mage is the real one.<br /> <br /> Ancillary sensory input like scent can be masked by Life or duplicated with Matter, also both a lower levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, at that point you'd fuck yourself into a corner as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T05:58:04-07:00","id":896723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896719#post896719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, at that point you'd fuck yourself into a corner as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why? A mage is perfectly cognizant of his own spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:05:15-07:00","id":896729,"title":"","content":"The kind of sensory input you'd need to provide to overwhelm every sense of a werewolf would screw you up too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T06:13:31-07:00","id":896733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896729#post896729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kind of sensory input you'd need to provide to overwhelm every sense of a werewolf would screw you up too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily, particularly if the spell(s) were intended as sensory decoys which the casting mage could always distinguish as they would be the product of his own magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:19:06-07:00","id":896782,"title":"","content":"Invisibility should probably be handled just like the stronger blind tilt, which is also applicable to total darkness. And it would probably not just last for one action but as long as the spell holds. Being hit by an invisible attacker doesn't make you see him more than before, unless the spell breaks. You still can't see him, which is still covered by the full blinded tilt (not just one eye, or blurred vision)<br /> <br /> Against supernatural beings, a clash of wills could occur, obviously. And for werewolves, as it was stated, they can adapt to ignore any visual hinderance. Other supernatural beings might have similar powers, but not sure. For example, vampires with auspex could have a devotion to ignore blinded tilts, or some protean powers to also ignore vision impediments, or some Cruac ritual, etc. Even for humans you could probably develop fighting techniques to ignore or reduce the hinderances of fighting blind, but that might be a bit of a stretch (think of eastern movies, etc.)<br /> <br /> Concerning the werewolf senses: They need to use some sense, they are just not hindered if they can't use their visual sense by falling back on other senses. If there is no smell, sound or air movement (don't forget tactile senses), they are just as blind as everyone else. If you only mask a part of that, maybe work with the weaker version of blind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3278,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","user":"Tyloron","date":". 05-23-2016, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","name":"Tyloron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:24:44-07:00","id":896790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896636#post896636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see why you shouldn't be able to overwhelm the senses of something with supersenses. Or someone with normal senses for that matter.<br /> <br /> But yea, to completely evade a werewolf, you would need to do allot of hoopely jumps and snickedy sneakeeks :P</div> </div> </div> </div>You have to overwhelm all of the werewolf's senses at once, or the others compensate for it. It's in their rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:42:41-07:00","id":896806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896790#post896790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to overwhelm all of the werewolf's senses at once, or the others compensate for it. It's in their rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Including their sense of touch I imagine...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:55:55-07:00","id":896813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896806#post896806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including their sense of touch I imagine...</div> </div> </div> </div>Whiskers in the wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T07:57:15-07:00","id":896816,"title":"","content":"Being blinded vs not seeing your attacker is totally different in practice, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T10:49:36-07:00","id":896945,"title":"","content":"Aah, so Werewolves has a special rule that protects them.. Cheaters :P<br /> But okay.. Werewolves will be an exception to the rule then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T11:08:58-07:00","id":896975,"title":"","content":"Vampires have a similar, though not as powerful exception. 'Kindred do not suffer normal vision penalties for being in the dark, and can compensate with hearing. In full darkness, they only suffer a -2 die penalty to rolls that require vision...They can hear heartbeats at three yards or meters per dot of Blood Potency. Upon Embrace, a vampire's sense of smell attunes to the scent of blood. A vampire can smell the presence of blood from about ten yards or meters per dot of Blood Potency without rolling. Multiply this range by her Auspex dots.' Between these exceptions, a foe that protects itself simply by making itself invisible will be surprised when coming up against a vampire. Fortunately abilities like Obfuscate and, presumably, something in the Mind Arcana like a variant of Incognito Presence, work off the target's mind and not shielding the self.<br /> <br /> The enhanced senses of Vampires and Werewolves have been given some nice rules in second edition, very powerful but often overlooked. Mage Sight had a similarly nice change. I don't know if Changelings or Prometheans have any such advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-23-2016, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T17:34:43-07:00","id":897376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyloron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=896782#post896782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invisibility should probably be handled just like the stronger blind tilt, which is also applicable to total darkness. And it would probably not just last for one action but as long as the spell holds. Being hit by an invisible attacker doesn't make you see him more than before, unless the spell breaks. You still can't see him, which is still covered by the full blinded tilt (not just one eye, or blurred vision)<br /> <br /> Against supernatural beings, a clash of wills could occur, obviously. And for werewolves, as it was stated, they can adapt to ignore any visual hinderance. Other supernatural beings might have similar powers, but not sure. For example, vampires with auspex could have a devotion to ignore blinded tilts, or some protean powers to also ignore vision impediments, or some Cruac ritual, etc. Even for humans you could probably develop fighting techniques to ignore or reduce the hinderances of fighting blind, but that might be a bit of a stretch (think of eastern movies, etc.)<br /> <br /> Concerning the werewolf senses: They need to use some sense, they are just not hindered if they can't use their visual sense by falling back on other senses. If there is no smell, sound or air movement (don't forget tactile senses), they are just as blind as everyone else. If you only mask a part of that, maybe work with the weaker version of blind.</div> </div> </div> </div>A combined Forces/Mind should do it. Or Forces/Life to spoof odor. Forces takes care of sight, sound and heat. Mind is obvious in that fools the victim into thinking you aren't there even though you are. So it's probably the best bet to get around a werewolf's or vampire's special exceptions.<br /> <br /> The ironclad solution would require a combined spell spell using Forces/Life/Mind but I imagine you'd have to be at least mid level in gnosis to try it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 05-23-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T18:26:28-07:00","id":897405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=897376#post897376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A combined Forces/Mind should do it. Or Forces/Life to spoof odor. Forces takes care of sight, sound and heat. Mind is obvious in that fools the victim into thinking you aren't there even though you are. So it's probably the best bet to get around a werewolf's or vampire's special exceptions.<br /> <br /> The ironclad solution would require a combined spell spell using Forces/Life/Mind but I imagine you'd have to be at least mid level in gnosis to try it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even then, doing so amid combat, with 2 or more Uratha around, bigger than size 5 and possibly at Kuruth? Very, very hard to pull off. Nevermind the Human packmates. Screwing with packs is decidedly a bad idea for mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:08:47-07:00","id":897928,"title":"","content":"Why is the main point here &quot;werewolves this and werewolves that&quot;? I also wrote about it, but it is not the main question asked here. And any mage going unprepared against werewolves is a bad idea. This isn't new.<br /> <br /> Anyway, back to topic: I have no firsthand experience at blindness or fighting an invisible foe, so I can't really judge the practical difference. In most cases, it probably depends on the surroundings. If you stand in an empty parking lot or a factory hall, it probably doesn't make much of a difference, because the attacker could be all around you. It might be easier, if you stand in a corner, because then you know that there are two walls in your back.However, you could also know that in total darkness/blind.<br /> <br /> If you think the full blindness tilt for every action is too strong, you could just apply it to the first attack, and then the attacker's position can be estimated and just gets the moditications of the weaker blind tilt. But I would then also allow the invisible mage to reposition / go hiding / sneak to gain the full blinded tilt for one acation again.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if this doesn't happen with just the mage and one victim (who can concentrate on the invisible opponent), but maybe a bar fight or in a crowd, I would consider that pretty much as the full blinded tilt for every action.<br /> <br /> Maybe the tilt should be rephrased &quot;no clue where the attack comes from&quot; (stronger blinded tilt) and &quot;blurred vision, confused senses, etc.&quot;(weaker blinded tilt)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3278,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","user":"Tyloron","date":". 05-24-2016, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3278-tyloron","name":"Tyloron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-24T10:46:54-07:00","id":897980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kumiko</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=897376#post897376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A combined Forces/Mind should do it. Or Forces/Life to spoof odor. Forces takes care of sight, sound and heat. Mind is obvious in that fools the victim into thinking you aren't there even though you are. So it's probably the best bet to get around a werewolf's or vampire's special exceptions.<br /> <br /> The ironclad solution would require a combined spell spell using Forces/Life/Mind but I imagine you'd have to be at least mid level in gnosis to try it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Forces/Matter could get you the effects of what is essentially a magical version of a mundane flashbag, but based on the various practices wouldn't it be simpler to just make a flashbag and use <i>shielding</i> to avoid being affected? Also couldn't the reaches you saved by using a simpler effect pay off by having it be better in another way?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T23:43:31-07:00","id":975394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=897405#post897405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even then, doing so amid combat, with 2 or more Uratha around, bigger than size 5 and possibly at Kuruth? Very, very hard to pull off. Nevermind the Human packmates. Screwing with packs is decidedly a bad idea for mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAgreed unless you're Thymus with Spirit 4/5. Then it's a bad idea for them to fuck with you. I was just talking about invisibility and what some boneheaded AA might do if they didn't just kick back and use their order merit for a scene for some reason I can't figure out like going Michone. or stupider?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2682,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","user":"Kumiko","date":". 09-24-2016, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:10:38-07:00","id":975405,"title":"","content":"Prime Veiling lets you hide supernatural things and people from others. Spirit Veiling lets you hide yourself from Spirits.<br /> <br /> Is there any reason you couldn't just use Life Shielding to either hide yourself as a Living Thing or hide yourself from other Living Things, as these are established uses of Veiling?<br /> <br /> Then you don't even have to worry about enhanced senses. You're masked from all their senses at once. In fact, passive abilities like the Wolf Senses outright fail without a Clash of Wills based on the precedent set by the other spells. And there's nothing that says combat breaks Veiling spells that I've found.<br /> <br /> People might be overthinking things a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T00:20:11-07:00","id":975408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/895616-invisibility-combat?p=975405#post975405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime Veiling lets you hide supernatural things and people from others. Spirit Veiling lets you hide yourself from Spirits.<br /> <br /> Is there any reason you couldn't just use Life Shielding to either hide yourself as a Living Thing or hide yourself from other Living Things, as these are established uses of Veiling?<br /> <br /> Then you don't even have to worry about enhanced senses. You're masked from all their senses at once. In fact, passive abilities like the Wolf Senses outright fail without a Clash of Wills based on the precedent set by the other spells. And there's nothing that says combat breaks Veiling spells that I've found.<br /> <br /> People might be overthinking things a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPossibly. I never knew that. If true an easy Force/Prime spell might work depending on interpretation. But myself? I don't buy it. I think Life would have to be in the equation for Uratha while Prime spoofs your aura.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2682-kumiko","name":"Kumiko","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T05:11:04-07:00","id":975475,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1692_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1692\" data-vbnamecard=\"1692\">Maina</a> yeah, you coud do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}